From: Codex Executor <codex-executor@local>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 17:27:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/22] sheet route: cooperative memory budget for the Schur
 stage

Memory, not CPU, bounds how many labels a machine runs at once: the
Schur stage of a thick cell peaks above 30 GB while the surface and port
stages need well under 1 GB, and the surface stage is single-threaded.
Running five jobs at a time under a 128 GiB cgroup therefore leaves most
cores idle.

MemoryBudget lets jobs run freely through the cheap stages and reserve
their estimated Schur memory (45 MB per 1000 fine Tet10 dof, from the
mesh) before the expensive one.  Reservations are per-process files
summed under a directory lock; a reservation whose process is gone counts
for nothing, so a killed job cannot leak budget.  produce_sheet_label
takes --memory-budget-dir / --memory-budget-gb and records the wait and
the reservation in the receipt.
